# U2 (SOFT, card M only): the canonical-rule probe (optimisation/ttnn-op/canon_probe). Every one of the 65,536 bfloat16 bit patterns, 64 tiles of a (1, 32, 2048) TILE tensor (row r, column c holds the pattern r * 2048 + c), goes through the row mover's canonical modes 3 and 4 (gdn_rows_dma_tp.cpp, CANON_DENORM=1: +0 where the exponent field is zero)
# and through the served path (the untilize / slice / tilize round trip on rows 0-15 and 16-31, and the served tile slice that starts inside a tile), compared as int16 bit patterns; the CPU model of the rule is held against the served path too, and the raw modes (1 and 2) are the control (a copy must be exact).
# WHAT IT DECIDES: whether V2, V1, WC and K5-B rest on a CONSTRUCTION (the rule is proved over every pattern: X-construct) or only on what the audits observed on real data (X-obs); it is a prerequisite of WC in W3. The report also lists the patterns the served path changes (the rule as observed) and the input fidelity: a pattern the runtime's upload alters is not exercised, and the verdict then reads PASS-PARTIAL with the count.
# READ: 'U2_CANON verdict=PASS' (every comparison differing=0 over all 65,536 patterns); PASS-PARTIAL says how many patterns reached the device unchanged (the rule is then proved over those and observed on none of the rest); FAIL names the first 64 differing patterns (a pattern class the mover and the served path treat differently: V2/V1/WC/K5-B then rest on observed data only and the kernel's rule needs a new build); NOT-RUN carries the error text. One chip only: the four chips run the same kernel on the same bytes, and A1's audits cover them on real data.
# Duration (estimate): 20 min (container timeout 1 h; the probe's own watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the card is resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# CARD M ONLY, BEFORE ANY QUAD JOB: the cardm step runs one board; it never runs while a quad step holds the cards, and the harness refuses while anything else can reach the board.
# The harness's container turns the image's C2 boot hook off (QWEN_C2_SERVING=0) and unsets the baked four-card mesh descriptor (env -u TT_MESH_GRAPH_DESC_PATH); the workflow's
# cardm step waits for other CI's buildx builders instead of refusing the window. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is the image B0 built (a harness mounts this checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs).
C2_SUPERSEDED_BY=tp4-w2ln-jobs
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/canon_probe/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
